    {
      "id": "intro_t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 14,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 1772,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "f0",
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1397871145,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 103694313,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793750000000,
      "created": 1793750000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What this chart is about\n- Northbridge Cycles (Pune, Maharashtra) ordered 18,000 battery packs from Voltway Cells (Gujarat) at Rs.1,276.80 each (order PO/2026/01120). Both are Indian residents;\n  GST is 18%.\n- The contract says: the price on the delivery date applies; a cash discount counts from the delivery date and reduces the GST too; defective goods must be claimed from\n  Voltway within 2 days; goods broken in transit are Northbridge's risk, claimed from its insurer.\n- Voltway's price became Rs.1,332.80 on 1st October. The packs arrived on 2nd October; 300 were broken in transit. Invoice 4471 bills 18,000 at Rs.1,332.80. It is due on\n  16th November; Northbridge would normally pay it in the 20th November run.\n- On 7th October Voltway emailed better terms (0.5% if paid within 15 days of delivery, 0.25% within 30) and called Emma the next day. Voltway never learns about\n  Northbridge's holds or internal steps.\n- This invoice takes Voltway's purchases this year past Rs.50 lakh, so TDS starts (Income-tax Act 2025, s.393(1), formerly 194Q).\n- Frame 1 (the top band): today, by hand, with red notes where it goes wrong. Frame 2 (the band under it, same phases): with the assistant in place from the start. The\n  agent drafts every entry, and a person approves or amends each one within 24 hours (frame 3). Every morning it checks the bank's emails against the bank statement (frame\n  4). The tables (money, jobs, guardrails, tests) are in CAPSTONE.md.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "intro",
      "originalText": "What this chart is about\n- Northbridge Cycles (Pune, Maharashtra) ordered 18,000 battery packs from Voltway Cells (Gujarat) at Rs.1,276.80 each (order PO/2026/01120). Both are Indian residents;\n  GST is 18%.\n- The contract says: the price on the delivery date applies; a cash discount counts from the delivery date and reduces the GST too; defective goods must be claimed from\n  Voltway within 2 days; goods broken in transit are Northbridge's risk, claimed from its insurer.\n- Voltway's price became Rs.1,332.80 on 1st October. The packs arrived on 2nd October; 300 were broken in transit. Invoice 4471 bills 18,000 at Rs.1,332.80. It is due on\n  16th November; Northbridge would normally pay it in the 20th November run.\n- On 7th October Voltway emailed better terms (0.5% if paid within 15 days of delivery, 0.25% within 30) and called Emma the next day. Voltway never learns about\n  Northbridge's holds or internal steps.\n- This invoice takes Voltway's purchases this year past Rs.50 lakh, so TDS starts (Income-tax Act 2025, s.393(1), formerly 194Q).\n- Frame 1 (the top band): today, by hand, with red notes where it goes wrong. Frame 2 (the band under it, same phases): with the assistant in place from the start. The\n  agent drafts every entry, and a person approves or amends each one within 24 hours (frame 3). Every morning it checks the bank's emails against the bank statement (frame\n  4). The tables (money, jobs, guardrails, tests) are in CAPSTONE.md.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "key",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 460,
      "width": 2276.3,
      "height": 75.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "f0",
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 155555738,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1763673107,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793750000000,
      "created": 1793750000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "[Human] = a person does it    [Agent] = Ask Northbridge does it    [System] = Ledgerline does it on its own    Diamond = a decision\nThick line = the path invoice 4471 takes.  Thin line = the other answers.  Red = how it goes wrong today.  Green = how the assistant fixes it.  → approval loop = the entry goes through frame 3.  Arrows show order in time.\nEach band reads left to right, phase by phase; \"continues in phase N\" joins the columns.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "[Human] = a person does it    [Agent] = Ask Northbridge does it    [System] = Ledgerline does it on its own    Diamond = a decision\nThick line = the path invoice 4471 takes.  Thin line = the other answers.  Red = how it goes wrong today.  Green = how the assistant fixes it.  → approval loop = the entry goes through frame 3.  Arrows show order in time.\nEach band reads left to right, phase by phase; \"continues in phase N\" joins the columns.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
